          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-12 mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Interesting Facts</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <li>Hong Kong salaries tax rates start as low as 2% under the progressive system, making it one of the most favorable income tax regimes in the world.</li>
            <li>The basic allowance for 2024/25 is HK$132,000, meaning the first HK$132,000 of your net chargeable income is completely tax-free.</li>
            <li>Taxpayers can choose between the progressive rate and the standard rate each year, and they should always pick the method that produces the lower tax bill.</li>
            <li>Mandatory Provident Fund (MPF) contributions are deductible up to HK$18,000 per year for each of the employee and employer portions.</li>
            <li>The IRD's territorial basis means that employment income sourced outside Hong Kong is generally not taxable, even if you are a Hong Kong resident.</li>
          </ul>

